---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE, HOST, SITE_NAME } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="The Font Finder AI privacy policy: images are processed entirely in your browser, no accounts, no tracking cookies, minimal data collection."
  path="/privacy"
  image="/og.png"
>
  <div class="container-page py-10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Privacy" }]} />

      <header class="mt-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-display-lg">Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-caption text-mute">Last updated: January 2026</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose-doc mt-8">
        <p>
          {SITE_NAME} (<strong>{HOST}</strong>) is built around a simple promise: images you run through the font finder
          never leave your device. This policy explains what we do (and don't) collect, in plain language.
        </p>

        <h2>Images and identification</h2>
        <p>
          The font identification runs entirely in your browser. The image you upload or paste is decoded with the browser's
          canvas APIs and compared against a pre-loaded signature index served with the page. We have no server that
          receives, stores, or processes your images, and the tool makes no network request containing them.
        </p>

        <h2>Data we collect</h2>
        <p>
          The site is static and server-rendered. We do not require accounts and we do not use advertising or tracking
          cookies. The only data stored on your device is:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>your theme preference (light or dark) in <code>localStorage</code>, set by the theme toggle; and</li>
          <li>normal browser caching of the static site and the font signature index.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Fonts and external services</h2>
        <p>
          Specimen fonts are loaded from Google Fonts when you view the library or results. Loading a web font causes a
          request to Google's font servers with your IP address, subject to Google's own privacy policy. We do not control
          or have access to that data. Where we link to third-party foundries or font sellers, their sites are governed by
          their own policies.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We may use privacy-respecting, aggregate analytics (such as server log counts of page views) to understand which
          pages are useful. These do not include image content, per-user identifiers, or cross-site tracking.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          The service is general-audience and not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
          information from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top of this page. Material changes will be noted here.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>